# Docker reads this file from the build CONTEXT ROOT, and its patterns are resolved relative to
# that root, not to this file's directory. In an lt-monorepo the context is the repo root, so
# `projects/app/.dockerignore` is never consulted at all. Every pattern that must also hit
# `projects/*` therefore uses a `**/` glob, so the same list works for a standalone build
# (context = this directory) and for a copy placed at the monorepo root. The Dockerfile
# additionally removes the build-read artefacts, so a missing root .dockerignore can never bake
# a developer's local config into an image.

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.npm

# Build output and the Angular CLI cache. The globstar is load-bearing: docker anchors a
# slash-free pattern at the CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare `.output` would exclude nothing once this
# template sits at `projects/app` in a monorepo.
**/.angular
**/.output
**/.output-check
**/.output-test
# Catch-all: `NG_OUTPUT_DIR` makes `.output-<x>` trivial to spawn.
**/.output-*
**/dist

# IDE / tooling
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.claude
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# Logs (`**/*.log.*` for rotated logs such as `.lt-dev/app.log.1`)
**/*.log
**/*.log.*
**/npm-debug.log*

# `lt dev`'s runtime directory: detached server logs and scratch state.
**/.lt-dev

# Testing. A Playwright trace records the full request log of the failing test, session cookie
# included. The specs are not needed by the build either.
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.vitest
**/tests

# Environment: a developer's local config must never reach an image. `.env*` covers the whole
# family, `.env.example` included (no build step reads it).
**/.env*

# Git
**/.git
**/.gitignore

# Docker
**/Dockerfile*
**/docker-compose*
**/.dockerignore

# Documentation
**/*.md
!README.md

# Misc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.tgz
